Error [jet.CompileTimeNumberParameter]: `N` is a compile-time number parameter, which this compiler does not support yet.
  --> tests/ui/prep_number_param_unsupported.jet:4:25
    |
  4 | Packet: struct<comptime N: Int> {
    |                         ^
 Why: `<comptime N: Int>` is the ratified declaration grammar, but number-parameter substitution, instance identity and layout are not implemented.
 Fix: Use a type parameter, or pass the number as an ordinary argument or field until number parameters ship.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0390

